# Notes on the Vercel setup live here rather than in vercel.json, because that
# file is schema-checked and rejects any key it does not recognise — including
# a "//" comment key. This file allows comments; that one does not.
#
# vercel.json turns on cleanUrls so pages address each other as /state rather
# than /state.html, matching how the links are already written and how
# Cloudflare serves them. There is no build step: the folder is the site.
#
# Below: Cloudflare's Pages Function. It does not run on Vercel, and uploading it
# would publish the source as a plain file the browser could download. When
# accounts and payments are connected here, this gets ported to an api/
# directory instead — see the note in vercel.json.
functions
